## Problem

On Windows with real-time antivirus, the first launch of a freshly downloaded `cloudflared.exe` takes 20 to 27 s while the scanner inspects it. Installing the relay client checked the download with a `cloudflared version` probe capped at 10 s, so the install failed with "The downloaded relay client binary did not run." Every retry downloads into a new `.install-*` directory, so every retry is a first launch again and fails the same way. Without the relay, the phone cannot pair to a desktop that only listens on 127.0.0.1.

Reproduced on Linux with the real installer: the release asset is a script whose first launch per file sleeps N s. On main, N = 20 and N = 27 both fail after 10 s, and a retry fails again. N = 3 installs.

## Change

The probe body (spawn `version`, parse, time out to `null`) becomes `runVersionProbe(path, timeout)`. The cached status/resolve probe still calls it with the 10 s `VERSION_PROBE_TIMEOUT`. Post-download validation calls it directly with a new 2-minute `INSTALL_VALIDATION_TIMEOUT`. The temp path is unique per attempt, so the cache never helped there. Error reasons and messages are unchanged.

## Scope and approval

Fixes pingdotgg/t3code#27409

