#48 was merged while it still targeted #47's branch (`feat/availability-calibration-deadline-alerts`), so the replay never reached `main`. This PR brings it to `main`, plus one new commit: each season is played from several start gameweeks.

## Summary
- **`scripts/analysis/manager_replay.py`** plays the ML manager's planner through past seasons:
  - **`project`** trains the points model on the seasons before each replayed one, the way production trains it. At every deadline it rebuilds what the live pipeline would have had and runs `predict_next_gw`'s own code on it:
    - earlier matches;
    - that gameweek's prices, ownership and transfers;
    - the last FPL snapshot;
    - only odds and snapshots from before the deadline.
  - **`plan`** plays each season under planner variants, from every start gameweek in `--start-gws` (new; default `1,5,9,13` in the workflow). `services/fpl_manager` validates, applies and scores every entry with the actual points under today's rules.
  - **`report`** pools every season-and-start path (new). It shows each season's total over its starts, the difference from the reference with a paired bootstrap over gameweeks, and how many paths each variant beats the reference on (new). It also shows how projection quality falls with the gameweeks ahead.
- **Manager replay workflow** (`.github/workflows/manager-replay.yml`): one job per season, projecting once from the earliest start. With 17 variants from four starts, a job takes about 2 hours.
- **Planner:** new `TRANSFER_MARGIN` and `HIT_MARGIN` constants, both 0, so behaviour is unchanged.

## Results so far (single start per run; recorded in CLAUDE.md under "Season replay")
- **First run** (run 41089319406: v4, 2022-23..2024-25 from GW1):
  - current settings: 6942 points;
  - never transferring: 5559 (-12.1 a gameweek), so transfers and chips earn about 460 points a season;
  - no chips: about -87 a season.
- **Transfer margin:** a 1-point margin was ahead in every season from GW1 (+1.98 a gameweek [-0.06, +3.97]). From GW9 (run 41112157292) it was -0.56 a gameweek. **Production keeps both margins at 0.**
- **Why several starts:** changing the start moved a variant's lead by up to 180 points, so a single path per season can't measure effects of a point or two a gameweek. After this merges, a dispatch with the defaults gives the pooled comparison.

## Notes
- **Running it:** `workflow_dispatch` only works once the workflow is on `main`. The two earlier runs were started by a temporary push trigger (added and removed in two commits here) and by the throwaway branch `replay-run/margins-gw9`, which can be deleted. After this merges, start the workflow from the Actions tab.
- **Known differences from live:**
  - the fixture list is the season as played, so doubles and blanks are known 4 gameweeks ahead;
  - the model is trained once per season;
  - a few gameweeks a season have no snapshot.

